{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Kf5KSYUefNLamrgvR9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written it so it faces the last campaign directly: many readers were refunded three years ago, and a refund shows their money is safe this time. The pitch is about 290 words.\n\n<final_document>\n**Bring Back the Majestic**\n\nThe Majestic on Main Street has been dark since 2022. The nearest cinema is now 38 miles away. When the Majestic closed, it was still selling about 180 tickets a week.\n\nWe can reopen it by Thanksgiving. We need $85,000 to replace the projector and sound system and repair the roof. If we raise it, the building's owner will rent the Majestic to us for $1 a year for ten years.\n\nSome of you remember our last campaign. Three years ago we asked for $120,000, reached $47,000, and returned every dollar. This time is different:\n\n- **The goal is $35,000 lower.**\n- **A local bank has pledged $25,000** if we raise the rest by June 30.\n- **Three local businesses have already pledged $11,000** in writing.\n- **46 volunteers have signed up** to run the box office and the snack bar.\n\nThat leaves **$49,000** to raise from our community between May 1 and June 30.\n\n**Your pledge is safe.** This campaign is all-or-nothing. If we don't reach $85,000 by June 30, every pledge is returned in full, just as last time.\n\n**You'll see where the money goes.** If we succeed, we'll post a public spending report at the town library every three months.\n\n**One honest note:** we can't promise new films in their opening week. Release dates are set by the film distributors, not by us. We can promise a screen, a seat and a night out without a 76-mile round trip.\n\nEvery pledge, large or small, brings the Majestic closer to opening its doors. Pledge by June 30, and let's turn the lights back on.\n\nRuth Albers\nChair, volunteer group to reopen the Majestic\n</final_document>\n\nBefore it goes out:\n\n- **The $49,000 figure** assumes the businesses' $11,000 counts toward the $60,000 the public needs to raise, not on top of it. Please check that.\n- **The roof estimate may rise by up to 15%.** I left this out because I don't have a plan to pair it with. If the cost goes up, readers will ask who covers it. Decide before May 1 whether you'd cover it with the bank money or a stretch goal, or whether the budget already has room. Then a short sentence on it could go in.\n- **Reward tiers:** once you settle them, add a short section before the closing line.\n- **Your group's name:** add it to the signature line if it has one, along with the platform link."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1186,"cache_read_input_tokens":10136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1186},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8ef2373-ab8a-41b1-9beb-08155911556a","uuid":"7a9bde8d-833f-4346-a843-a29a334ec2c2","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:32:52.225Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7Kf5B1V5msvdznM6cfY"}
